{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QBCDkv69Wix7PzY4tgAFaR","type":"tool_result","content":"3915\t\tfor _, criterion := range bundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria {\n3916\t\t\tif criterion.Required {\n3917\t\t\t\trequired[criterion.ID] = criterion\n3918\t\t\t}\n3919\t\t}\n3920\t\t// The findings this attestation records, so a criterion disposed as\n3921\t\t// `finding` can be checked against them. The CLI parser already refused a\n3922\t\t// criterion naming a finding it does not record; the Store did not, so any\n3923\t\t// other caller — a Store client, a signed import, a reuse — could approve a\n3924\t\t// criterion that explicitly did not pass while filing nothing. A signature\n3925\t\t// authenticates bytes; it does not repair a reference to something that\n3926\t\t// does not exist (spec pose-abm-review-soundness).\n3927\t\trecordedFindings := map[string]bool{}\n3928\t\tfor _, finding := range att.Findings {\n3929\t\t\trecordedFindings[finding.ID] = true\n3930\t\t}\n3931\t\tsealedClasses := map[string]bool{}\n3932\t\tfor _, ev := range bundle.Payload.Evidence {\n3933\t\t\tsealedClasses[ev.EvidenceClass] = true\n3934\t\t}\n3935\t\tjudgmentGoverned, _ := BundleGovernedBy(bundle, \"explicit-judgment\")\n3936\t\tif structuralGoverned, _ := BundleGovernedBy(bundle, \"structural-causality\"); structuralGoverned {\n3937\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, s.reviewStructuralCausalityBlockers(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref, bundle.Payload.Plan.Structure, required, att.Criteria)...)\n3938\t\t}\n3939\t\tif closeoutGoverned, _ := BundleGovernedBy(bundle, CausalityCloseoutContract); closeoutGoverned {\n3940\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, s.reviewCausalityCloseoutBlockers(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref, bundle.Payload.Plan.Structure, bundle.Payload.Plan.Band, required, att.Criteria)...)\n3941\t\t}\n3942\t\t// Validation evidence can be required by implementation components even\n3943\t\t// when no delivery target is declared. A target-gated tool must use the\n3944\t\t// sealed declaration, not the broader evidence requirement.\n3945\t\thasDeliveryTarget := len(bundle.Payload.Scope.Deliveries) > 0\n3946\t\tif bundle.Payload.Scope.Kind != \"spec\" {\n3947\t\t\ttoolScope, _ := ParseScopeRef(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n3948\t\t\ttoolGraph, _ := s.GetDeliveryIntegrity(\"\")\n3949\t\t\thasDeliveryTarget = s.reviewScopeRequiresValidationEvidence(toolScope, bundle.Payload.Plan, toolGraph)\n3950\t\t}\n3951\t\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n3952\t\tnotApplicable := 0\n3953\t\tfor _, criterion := range att.Criteria {\n3954\t\t\tif seen[criterion.ID] {\n3955\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"duplicate criterion \"+criterion.ID)\n3956\t\t\t}\n3957\t\t\tseen[criterion.ID] = true\n3958\t\t\tplanned, known := required[criterion.ID]\n3959\t\t\tif !known {\n3960\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"unknown criterion \"+criterion.ID)\n3961\t\t\t}\n3962\t\t\tif criterion.Disposition != \"passed\" && criterion.Disposition != \"not-applicable\" && criterion.Disposition != \"finding\" {\n3963\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"criterion \"+criterion.ID+\" has invalid disposition\")\n3964\t\t\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f88eaf94-50c5-41a5-9e25-d5bcef8b3bff","timestamp":"2026-11-26T05:37:43.081Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-349050671/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go","content":"\tfor _, criterion := range bundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria {\n\t\tif criterion.Required {\n\t\t\trequired[criterion.ID] = criterion\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// The findings this attestation records, so a criterion disposed as\n\t// `finding` can be checked against them. The CLI parser already refused a\n\t// criterion naming a finding it does not record; the Store did not, so any\n\t// other caller — a Store client, a signed import, a reuse — could approve a\n\t// criterion that explicitly did not pass while filing nothing. A signature\n\t// authenticates b